'use strict';
// data/voice/dialog-ch3.js — Chapter 3 spoken dialogue clips, keyed 'voice|exact text' (data/dialog-cast.js). Built from the
// Chapter Voice Baker with claude/voice-merge-dialog.js; do not hand-edit.
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"tnb|Go. Hug the girls for me. I will be right here, pot-sitive.":"","sal|Airport. Love it. We will be there in twenty minutes. Or two hours. Nobody knows.":"","tnb|Well, well... this is where I get off. Glaze firing tomorrow, call time at five, and somebody has to water your plants.":"","tom|Worth it.":"","tom|Six hours. Then two small people will jump on me at full speed.":"","tom|Long Island. Nice and quiet. For about four more seconds.":"","grace|Tata! You are BACK! AGAIN!":"","rose|Did you bring me a palm tree?":"","grace|Did you miss us? Say a big number.":"","tom|A very big number. The biggest one.":"","tom|I brought you a picture of a palm tree.":"","rose|...That is ALMOST a palm tree.":"","grace|Tata! Boppy has been waiting by his window since BREAKFAST. He has his fishing hat on.":"","tom|Then we had better go help him not catch one.":"","rose|He said if you were late he would catch the fish without you. He has never caught a fish.":"","deedee|Back already! Look at you. Did they feed you out there? Never mind. I will feed you.":"","boppy|Tom. Good. Sit down. No. Do not sit down. We are going fishing.":"","deedee|Nobody believes him.":"","rose|Boppy, is the Whisker Perch real?":"","boppy|The Whisker Perch. Whiskers like a cat. I saw it at Cattail Pier in 1994. Nobody believes me.":"","boppy|Real as my heartburn, kiddo.":"","grace|I am bringing a notebook. For science. And for proof.":"","boppy|And I am bringing THIS. My pepper jar. Homegrown, pickled in 1989. Older than your mother.":"","deedee|I have three pies in, so I am staying put. Do NOT let him eat peppers on an empty stomach.":"","boppy|I never eat peppers on an empty stomach. I eat them on a full stomach. Then it is empty.":"","oolong|Boppy! The usual? Ginger, peppermint, and a little honey for the stomach.":"","boppy|The stomach thanks you. The stomach is still complaining. But it thanks you.":"","tom|On Long Island? Nobody here pays double for anything.":"","oolong|The kettle says a man in a long coat has been buying up gold coins at Penny’s. Paying double. Never takes his hat off.":"","grace|You did. Forty times.":"","oolong|The kettle also says it will rain on Tuesday. The kettle is wrong a lot. Enjoy the pier.":"","rose|Can you still run that fast?":"","boppy|Then forty-one. First year of college. Cross country. Five miles through the woods, up the big hill, and I never breathed hard.":"","boppy|Last hill, I passed the whole field. Champion. They put my name on a plaque. The plaque is in a box. Somewhere.":"","rose|Race you to the pier, Boppy!":"","boppy|...Sure. Sure I can. I just choose not to. It is bad for the stomach.":"","grace|Last one there is a soggy sock!":"","tom|Boppy speed, everybody. We walk at Boppy speed.":"","boppy|Why is everybody walking like they are going to a fire? Slow down! My stomach is doing flips!":"","rose|I AM BEING QUIET.":"","boppy|This is the spot. Forty years, this spot. Now everybody be QUIET.":"","grace|Rose. Inside voice. Outside.":"","tom|Shhh. Quiet on the pier, everybody. Boppy has a whole system.":"","boppy|Tom holds the tackle box. I cast. The fish comes. Nobody talks. That is the system.":"","boppy|...Any minute now.":"","grace|It has been a minute. I wrote it down.":"","rose|Deedee said NO peppers.":"","boppy|Deedee is not here.":"","boppy|Snack. A pickled pepper settles the stomach.":"","bigone|BLORP.":"","rose|TATA! A FISH! A HUGE ONE! WITH A MUSTACHE!":"","bigone|Blorp. Something smells like peppers.":"","boppy|MY JAR!":"","boppy|That is no perch. That is OLD IRON-GILL. I saw him in 1994! I TOLD everybody!":"","bigone|GULP. Spicy. I love it. Bye.":"","boppy|Pickled in 1989. Nobody takes Boppy’s peppers. NOBODY.":"","boppy|He went west. Into the Whispering Marsh. Come on. And nobody walk fast.":"","rose|Tata, that sock has a FACE.":"","mudling|Squelch. Have you seen my other sock? It looks just like me. It is ALSO angry.":"","boppy|Marsh junk. Everything people drop out here ends up grumpy about it. Like me, at the DMV.":"","boppy|Up. Everybody up. Headcount. One, two, three, four. Good. Nobody is missing. Again.":"","boppy|Socks. Out here. Nobody keeps track of their socks anymore.":"","grace|Boppy, you are breathing kind of hard.":"","grump|Snarl. Somebody cast me badly in 1997. I have been in a knot ever since. Nobody gets past ME.":"","boppy|Excuse me? Nobody gets past ME. That is MY line. I was saying that at Rikers before you were a knot.":"","boppy|I am breathing EXACTLY as hard as I want to.":"","tom|We take it slow. Iron-Gill’s wake goes northwest, toward those big reeds.":"","boppy|That is what I said.":"","grace|Sundials cannot tell the wrong time. That is not how sundials work.":"","boppy|The old reeds. When I was a kid we said there was a sundial back in there that told the wrong time.":"","tom|Then we ask it nicely to move. Iron-Gill is not keeping that jar.":"","boppy|You are sitting on the way to Sundial Hollow. Shove over.":"","log|Creak. This was a boardwalk once. Now it is MY spot. Everything catches on me here. I like it.":"","rose|Tata, it is a LOG with a BOOT.":"","log|Make me. Slowly. I am very heavy when wet. I am always wet.":"","grace|A secret boardwalk. Of course there is a secret boardwalk.":"","boppy|Not secret. Just old. Like me. Nobody comes back here anymore.":"","rose|Tata! Something shiny is stuck in it!":"","boppy|Sundial Hollow. I have not been back here since I was nine. It has not changed. It still says seven.":"","grace|It is the AFTERNOON. The sun is right there. Sundials cannot be wrong. That is not how sundials work.":"","tom|A coin. Wedged right under the pointer. Somebody pushed this in on purpose.":"","grace|It MOVED. Shadows do not move like that. I am writing this down. In pen.":"","boppy|Old gold. Keep that in your pocket, Tom. Penny will want to hear about it. Penny wants to hear about everything.":"","boppy|Now. The Deep Pool. That is where Iron-Gill goes to sulk.":"","boppy|You took my jar.":"","bigone|Blorp. The old man. And his small, loud friends.":"","boppy|The Deep Pool. Nobody has ever seen the bottom. My father said it goes all the way to Ohio.":"","boppy|He is a FISH, kiddo.":"","rose|Boppy, he is sad! And spicy!":"","bigone|I took your jar. Forty years you sit on that pier and you never once come to visit. You only ever bring HOOKS.":"","tom|Quiet on the pier, everybody.":"","boppy|Tom. Tackle box. We do this the old way.":"","boppy|Headcount. One, two, three, four. Good.":"","bigone|Blorp. Fine. FINE. Take your jar. It was too spicy anyway.":"","boppy|He belches every third turn, Tom. Heal right after. When he dives, hit the water hard, or do our Tombo.":"","boppy|My jar. Still sealed. Still hot.":"","boppy|And look at that. Forty years, and I finally caught Old Iron-Gill.":"","grace|Technically he caught your jar, and then we caught him. I am writing it down anyway. For proof.":"","boppy|Put the date. Put the time. Use the sundial. It works now.":"","boppy|Go on, you old bucket. Catch and release. I will come by. No hooks.":"","rose|Boppy, can we go home now? I want to tell Deedee EVERYTHING.":"","boppy|Everything except the pepper part.":"","rose|ESPECIALLY the pepper part.":"","deedee|There they are! Well? Did anybody catch anything?":"","deedee|Nobody believed you.":"","boppy|Old Iron-Gill. Forty years, Dee. I TOLD everybody.":"","deedee|Did he.":"","grace|I have proof. It is in my notebook. With the time. From a sundial.":"","rose|Deedee! Boppy almost ate a PEPPER! On the pier! Before LUNCH!":"","boppy|...Almost is not eating. Almost is fine.":"","boppy|Slowly. Finally. Somebody in this family gets it.":"","deedee|Sit down, you. I made rhubarb crisp. Everybody sit. And eat SLOWLY.":"","tom|Best fishing trip ever. Nobody fell in. Mostly.":"","deedee|I love you all to the moon and back. Now eat.":"","bean|Boppy went by with a fishing rod and a jar of peppers.":"","bean|He was walking slower than me. Nobody walks slower than me. I collect slow walks too, now.":"","gus|Your father caught Old Iron-Gill? And let him GO? Forty years of telling that story, and now it is true.":"","gus|He came by the shack this morning. The fish, not your father. Just floated there. I think he wanted to say hello.":"","gus|You saw it? Old Iron-Gill? Forty years I have run this shack. I thought it was a story.":"","gus|Bait shack is open. Worms, minnows, and a sandwich I am not selling.":"","gus|It went west, into the marsh. The Whispering Marsh. The reeds talk out there. Mostly nonsense.":"","gus|Your father has been fishing this pier since before the pier. He has caught nothing. Very consistent.":"","gus|They say a catfish lives out there older than the boards. I say they say a lot.":"","oolong|The kettle is still going on about that man in the long coat. Gold coins. Paying double.":"","oolong|I told it to mind its own business. It is a kettle. It has no business.":"","mudling|Squelch. Have you seen my other sock? It looks just like me.":"","mudling|I fell off a clothesline in 1998. Nobody came looking.":"","mudling|Round 2. I am wetter now.":"","mudling|Squelch. I found a puddle. I feel great.":"","mudling|Round 3. I am wetter now.":"","mudling|Round 4. I am wetter now.":"","mudling|Round 5. I am wetter now.":"","mudling|...I am drying. Do not look at me.":"","mudling|Drip. Drip. Give me a minute. Drip.":"","toad|I watch the water all day. The water does not watch back.":"","toad|Bob. Bob. Bob. Nothing bites. Nothing EVER bites.":"","toad|Bob. I got a nibble once. It was you.":"","toad|Round 2. I have been practicing ducking.":"","toad|Round 3. I have been practicing ducking.":"","toad|Round 4. I have been practicing ducking.":"","toad|Round 5. I have been practicing ducking.":"","toad|...Bob. Bob. I am resting. Bob.":"","toad|Nothing is biting. Not even me.":"","grump|Every time somebody pulls on me, I get tighter. Think about that.":"","grump|Snarl. Somebody cast me badly in 1997. I have been in a knot ever since.":"","grump|I found another hook. I wear it now.":"","grump|Round 2. I am knottier.":"","grump|Round 3. I am knottier.":"","grump|Round 4. I am knottier.":"","grump|Round 5. I am knottier.":"","grump|Do not pull. Pulling makes it worse.":"","grump|...I am untangling. This could take years.":"","log|Every line in this marsh catches on me. Then everybody yells at me.":"","log|I was a nice branch once. Then I fell in.":"","log|I caught another boot. Left foot this time.":"","log|Round 2. I am heavier when wet. I am always wet.":"","log|Round 3. I am heavier when wet. I am always wet.":"","log|Round 4. I am heavier when wet. I am always wet.":"","log|...Zzz. Everyone gets caught on me. Nobody stays.":"","log|Round 5. I am heavier when wet. I am always wet.":"","log|I am soaking. I am always soaking.":"","bigone|Blorp. I am still burping peppers.":"","bigone|Every hook in this marsh has been in my lip once. I spat them all out.":"","bigone|BLORP. I am older than the pier. I am older than the old man.":"","bigone|Round 4. Bring the old man. I miss him.":"","bigone|Round 2. Bring the old man. I miss him.":"","bigone|Round 3. Bring the old man. I miss him.":"","bigone|Blorp. That pepper jar is still repeating on me.":"","bigone|The pool is deep. I will be at the bottom of it.":"","bigone|Round 5. Bring the old man. I miss him.":"","amy|Thirty science fair projects to grade. Thirty. Take Dad fishing. He has been asking since you landed.":"","deedee|Not this time, honey. I have three pies in and Boppy needs somebody to go fishing with. Take the girls.":"","sal|Airport? You just got here. Your father has called the depot four times asking if you landed.":"","sal|Something about a fish. He sounded very serious about the fish.":"","boppy|At Rikers I did the headcount. One, two, three, Tom. Everybody here.":"","boppy|Slow down! Who taught you to walk? I was a champion runner and I never went this fast.":"","boppy|My stomach is talking. It says no more peppers. My stomach is wrong.":"","boppy|That Grump owes me a fish. Tell him.":""});
